# FABLE-SONNET-LAST-OCCURRENCE-20260924-164: the author's rule (Q22.2, LMX_blog/2026-09-24.md,
# book Sfields, CORE S3.1) -- an unqualified name is its LAST occurrence, including repeated
# occurrences of the same name in one method body. `test\[N]arg` still counts in lexical (source)
# order; unqualified `test\arg` is `test\[lastIndex]arg`.
#
# Measured (not assumed): read from a METHOD body (check(), here), `test\arg` already resolves
# through l2_own_seg_scan (l2_path_root -> l2_emit_path_to's method-root branch), whose
# scan-and-overwrite loop is last-occurrence by construction -- this fixture pins that this
# already holds correctly for the caller-is-a-method case, both read and write. It is NOT a
# mutation witness for this ticket's l2_own_find -> l2_own_find_last call-site routing (commit 2):
# every consumer of that routing checks l2_param_find (is this name a formal of the CURRENT
# method) before ever reaching own-find, and a repeated own row can currently only exist for a
# name that IS such a formal (the argument same-name-binding rule is the only legal way today to
# get more than one row for one name) -- so the formal fast path always wins first, and the
# routing change has no observable effect on any program this corpus can express today. It is
# still correct and closes two real first/last inconsistencies between code paths that would
# otherwise disagree if this ever becomes reachable (see steps/last-occurrence-inventory.md).
#
# poke9 writes arg's address BETWEEN the two named occurrences (unit_occ_snapshot_
# selector.lm2's mechanism) so occurrence 0 and occurrence 1 hold OBSERVABLY DIFFERENT values (9
# vs 2) -- without it (unit_occ_root_named.lm2's plain arg\1, arg\2 shape), occurrence 0
# re-syncs to the same final value at checkpoint time regardless of which row is "last", so
# first-vs-last is not observable there either.
#
# The READ-FROM-ROOT-LEVEL case is DIFFERENT and NOT covered here: unit_occ_root_named.lm2's own
# `test\arg` (called and read at root, not from inside a method) resolves to occurrence 0 (first),
# not last -- a genuine, separate, not-yet-fixed defect in the same l2_own_seg_scan mechanism,
# masked there only because that fixture's arg is argument-bound and both occurrences happen to
# publish the same value. See steps/last-occurrence-inventory.md and defects.md.
fn: poke9 (@: int p) int
    \p: 9
    return: 0
end: poke9

fn: test (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    poke9(@: arg)
    arg: 2
    return: 0
end: test

fn: check () int
    int: first
    int: second
    int: last
    test(0)
    first: test\[0]arg
    second: test\[1]arg
    last: test\arg
    if: first != 9
        return: 81
    if: second != 2
        return: 82
    if: last != 2
        return: 83
    test\arg: 5
    second: test\[1]arg
    first: test\[0]arg
    if: second != 5
        return: 84
    if: first != 9
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: check

return: check()
